      "sourceText": "מָה־ אֱנוֹשׁ כִּי־ תִזְכְּרֶנּוּ\nוּבֶן־ אָדָם כִּי תִפְקְדֶנּוּ׃\nוַתְּחַסְּרֵהוּ מְעַט מֵאֱלֹהִים\nוְכָבוֹד וְהָדָר תְּעַטְּרֵהוּ׃\nתַּמְשִׁילֵהוּ בְּמַעֲשֵׂי יָדֶיךָ\nכֹּל שַׁתָּה תַחַת־ רַגְלָיו׃\n צֹנֶה וַאֲלָפִים כֻּלָּם\nוְגַם בַּהֲמוֹת שָׂדָי׃\n צִפּוֹר שָׁמַיִם וּדְגֵי הַיָּם\nעֹבֵר אָרְחוֹת יַמִּים׃",
      "literalTranslation": "What is mortal man that you remember him, and the son of man that you attend to him? You made him lack a little from God, and with glory and splendor you crown him. You make him rule over the works of your hands; all you placed under his feet: sheep and cattle, all of them, and also beasts of the field; bird of heaven and fish of the sea, passing through the paths of seas.",
      "naturalTranslation": "What is mortal man that you remember him, or a human being that you care for him? Yet you made him only a little lower than God and crowned him with glory and splendor. You gave him rule over the works of your hands and placed everything beneath his feet: all sheep and cattle, and even the beasts of the field, the birds of the heavens and the fish of the sea, whatever passes along the paths of the seas.",
